{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ADR 0056 decision-3 remainder is COMPLETE and committed locally as 8aa86fe097 on feat/5e75-adr0056 (worktree /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-wt-5e75). NOT pushed to Gerrit per instruction.\n\nWhat landed: the fourth named extraction plus the post-call telemetry pair, moved from PydanticAIRunner.run() into the new leaf module src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py (build_agent_kwargs, log_call_success, record_call_spend), with tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py pinning the contracts.\n\nStatus of the 'four kwargs fragments' the previous agent flagged as remaining: all four were in fact already applied in the working tree when this session picked the work up — (1) the tool_step_limit convergence rewrite, (2) the kwargs dict literal, (3) the 'capabilities' key, (4) the 'model_settings' key. grep confirms zero kwargs mutation sites left in runner.py; run() now has a single build_agent_kwargs(...) call. Nothing deferred; no remaining fragments.\n\nTwo corrections made on top of the inherited state, both comment/test-only:\n- Removed test_runner_keeps_real_headroom_under_the_cap and the _RUNNER_HEADROOM_TARGET=700 constant from the new seam test. Re-adding a runner.py line-count assertion contradicts db7f / ADR 0058, which makes .github/module-size-limit.txt (800) the single authoritative ceiling. This accounts for the pass-count delta below.\n- Stripped stale line-count narrative ('699 LOC', 'one line of headroom') from the agent_call.py and seam-test docstrings.\n\nSeam judged unsafe to move, and deliberately left in run(): the _anthropic_web_search_capabilities call site. It is a runner module global that the suite patches via monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, ...); calling it from agent_call.py would resolve the name through that module's globals and silently defeat the patch. web_caps is therefore resolved in run() and passed in as a parameter.\n\nVerification (worktree venv, REBAR_GATE_REF=HEAD):\n- pytest -m 'not integration and not external' baseline 8829 passed / 31 skipped -> final 8828 passed / 31 skipped, 0 failed, exit 0. The -1 is exactly the deleted 700-LOC assertion.\n- make lint exit 0; make typecheck exit 0.\n- runner.py 658 LOC (from 699); agent_call.py 152 LOC (clears the 100-LOC anti-fragmentation floor); seam test 243 LOC.\n\nBase is deliberately stale; not rebased. Ticket left in_progress."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785688402511835001,"uuid":"253b1816-24a8-4dff-82b5-22e0a2ae0927"}